WEBVTT

00:02.223 --> 00:03.760
What can a walk reveal?

00:04.223 --> 00:06.690
GaitAI ForensicSearch.

00:07.208 --> 00:08.409
Two street recordings.

00:08.616 --> 00:09.433
One question:

00:09.896 --> 00:11.390
could this be the same person?

00:14.711 --> 00:16.039
Watch the white shoe.

00:16.119 --> 00:16.850
It lands.

00:17.143 --> 00:19.026
Then the same foot returns.

00:19.276 --> 00:21.370
That is one complete gait cycle.

00:24.315 --> 00:27.090
Gait cycle analysis finds repeating
movement.

00:28.012 --> 00:31.140
Pose estimation follows the joints through
each frame.

00:35.017 --> 00:38.053
Silhouette extraction separates the walker
from the scene.

00:38.431 --> 00:40.820
The outline changes as the body moves.

00:42.621 --> 00:45.357
Recording A contains two complete cycles.

00:45.394 --> 00:47.430
Recording B contains five.

00:49.020 --> 00:52.567
Gait phase alignment puts corresponding
moments side by side.

00:52.647 --> 00:54.061
These are phases of movement,

00:54.140 --> 00:56.180
not simultaneous camera times.

00:57.820 --> 01:01.196
The gait energy image averages the aligned
silhouettes.

01:01.403 --> 01:03.700
Brighter areas are occupied more often.

01:06.718 --> 01:08.900
It describes movement across frames,

01:08.980 --> 01:10.050
not identity.

01:10.317 --> 01:12.371
Cadence measures steps per minute.

01:12.535 --> 01:15.016
Ninety-nine point two in recording A.

01:15.234 --> 01:17.590
Ninety-six point four in recording B.

01:20.016 --> 01:22.650
A similar pace is only one observation.

01:26.022 --> 01:29.570
Recording B's left and right leg labels
are inconsistent.

01:29.734 --> 01:31.831
Step-time asymmetry is withheld.

01:31.996 --> 01:35.310
The software also withholds side-specific
joint curves.

01:35.637 --> 01:38.075
The measurements remain evidence to
examine.

01:38.240 --> 01:39.910
A walk can leave a trace.

01:40.160 --> 01:42.550
The conclusion must follow the evidence.

01:42.923 --> 01:45.390
GaitAI ForensicSearch.

01:45.441 --> 01:46.980
Request a Demonstration.
